go-to: menu

**Paramilitary groups:**

**[+ pps_militia_name +]**: the PPS self-defence organization. It protects meetings, offices, demonstrations and strikes against nationalist militias, communist militias and hostile state police. It begins as Milicja PPS and can be reorganized into Akcja Socjalistyczna. Historical details remain **TBD — historical research required**.

Active organized members: [+ pps_militia_strength +]

Militancy: [+ pps_militia_militancy : militancy +]

It is legal and not initially repressed. Trade-union cooperation improves coordination but never automatically adds union members to its strength.

**Temporary opponent model:** The following German formations still supply inherited numerical values. In the approved Polish design they represent communist militias, nationalist militias and state forces until their dedicated replacements are researched.

**Communist militias**: currently use the inherited RFB numerical model.

Strength: [+ rfb_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ rfb_militancy : militancy +]

**Nationalist militias — veteran formations**: currently use the inherited Stahlhelm numerical model.

Strength: [+ sh_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ sh_militancy : militancy +]

**Nationalist militias — mass formations**: currently use the inherited SA numerical model.

