@factions
go-to: menu

**Implemented PPS faction model**

The three currents below are gameplay abstractions. Their historical boundaries, memberships and opening proportions remain **TBD — historical research required**.

Overall dissent: [+ dissent_percent : dissent +]

**Centrum PPS**

The parliamentary democratic-socialist current emphasizes reform, workers' rights, defence of democracy and Polish independence.

Strength: [+ centrum_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ centrum_dissent : dissent +]

**Lewica PPS**

The left current emphasizes class struggle, faster socialisation, opposition to bourgeois governments and greater openness to extra-parliamentary pressure.

Strength: [+ lewica_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ lewica_dissent : dissent +]

**Piłsudczycy**

The Piłsudski-oriented current combines the independence tradition and social reform with a stronger-state, anti-communist outlook.

Strength: [+ pilsudczycy_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ pilsudczycy_dissent : dissent +]

**Affiliated trade unions — temporary compatibility model**

The inherited Labor values temporarily represent the trade-union power centre. It is separate from the three PPS factions and is excluded from their normalization and from overall party dissent. A researched ZSZ replacement remains planned.

Strength: [+ labor_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ labor_dissent : dissent +]

Inherited German card effects are transferred to the three active currents through a temporary compatibility bridge. The active advisers now use the semantic PPS faction fields directly. The remaining bridge is a gameplay device, not a claim that German and Polish factions were historically equivalent.

@advisers
title: PPS Advisers
go-to: menu

= PPS advisers

The PPS has three active adviser slots and a fourteen-person Polish adviser pool. Using any adviser action starts one shared six-month cooldown. Dismissing an adviser adds five dissent to their faction. A person's first appointment adds five faction strength; reappointing the same person does not repeat that bonus.

The January 1922 active team is **Ignacy Daszyński**, **Kazimierz Pużak**, and **Feliks Perl**.

**Centrum PPS:** Daszyński, Pużak, Perl, Mieczysław Niedziałkowski and Tomasz Arciszewski.

**Lewica PPS:** Zygmunt Zaremba, Kazimierz Czapiński, Adam Próchnik, Stanisław Dubois and Bolesław Drobner.

**Piłsudczycy:** Rajmund Jaworowski, Jędrzej Moraczewski, Bronisław Ziemięcki and Marian Malinowski.

Próchnik and Drobner enter the pool in 1928; Dubois enters in 1930. Perl leaves in April 1927. Daszyński leaves at the beginning of 1931 under the current year-only gameplay schedule.

Faction splits use named departures. A split only removes a person whose entry date has already arrived. Consequently, a Lewica split before 1930 does not prevent Dubois from entering in 1930.

Some approved adviser actions remain visibly marked as planned because Centrolew, Sanacja, municipal government, a Polish socialist economic programme, and formal PPS–KPP joint action do not yet have dedicated mechanics.


@figures
title: Figures and Charts
call: polish_opening_state
go-to: menu
on-display: {!
var data = Q.sejm_display_rows.map(function(row) {
    return {id: row.id, legend: row.name, name: row.name, seats: row.seats};
});
if (typeof d3 !== 'undefined' && typeof window !== 'undefined') {
    // get screen width
    var width = 500;
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50;
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("reichstag").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    }
    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#reichstag").datum(data).call(parliament);
    // Use the same palette as the legend/history, including the Other category.
    for (var row of Q.sejm_display_rows) {
        d3.select("#reichstag").selectAll(".seat." + row.id).style("fill", Q.sejm_chart_colors[row.id]);
    }

    // Accessible history tables use the same immutable list results as the
    // parliament. ChZJN is one row, never double-counted alongside its parties.
    var history = d3.select('#election_history');
    history.selectAll('*').remove();
    for (var election of Q.sejm_history) {
        history.append('h3').text(election.date + ' — ' + election.total + ' MPs' +
            (election.kind === 'legacy_continuation' ? ' (temporary continuation)' : ''));
        var table = history.append('table');
        table.append('caption').text('Recorded votes and seats; Inne aggregates separate small lists');
        table.append('thead').append('tr').selectAll('th')
            .data(['Electoral list / category', 'Votes %', 'MPs', 'Seats %']).enter().append('th').text(function(value) { return value; });
        var rows = table.append('tbody').selectAll('tr').data(election.rows).enter().append('tr');
        rows.selectAll('td').data(function(row) {
            return [row.name, row.votes.toFixed(2), row.seats, row.share.toFixed(2)];
        }).enter().append('td').text(function(value) { return value; });
    }

    // party support records should not have so many ticks
    if (!Q.historical_mode || Q.game_over) {
        var lines_2 = d3.linegraph(true, true,
            Q.parties,
            Q.party_colors,
            Q.party_names);
        lines_2.width(width).height(400);
        d3.select("#party_support_history").datum(Q.party_support_records).call(lines_2);
    }

    // economic stats
    var minInflation = d3.min(Q.economic_records, d => d.inflation);
    var maxUnemployment = d3.max(Q.economic_records, d => d.unemployment);
    var lines_3 = d3.linegraph(true, true, ['inflation', 'unemployment'],
            {'inflation': '#0000FF', 'unemployment': '#FF0000'},
            {'inflation': 'Inflation', 'unemployment': 'Unemployment'},
            maxUnemployment + 5, minInflation - 5, 21);
    lines_3.width(width).height(300);
    d3.select("#economic_history").datum(Q.economic_records).call(lines_3);
}
!}

= [+ parliament_heading +]

[? if opening_sejm_active : Each dot represents one MP in the approved 444-seat opening approximation, using August club shares from January. Percentages are rounded for display; these are not current opinion polls. ?]

[? if not opening_sejm_active : Each dot represents one MP in the recorded [+ sejm_total_seats +]-seat result, not current polling. Majority: [+ sejm_majority_required +] MPs. [? if sejm_has_chzjn : ChZJN is displayed as one bloc; ZLN and PSChD remain separate political parties. ?] ?]

{!<svg id="reichstag" style="width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

{!<table>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#8B0000'> </div></td><td>!} KPP {!</td><td>!} [+ kpp_sejm_display +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#E3000F; outline: 2px; outline-style: solid;'> </div></td><td>!} **PPS** {!</td><td>!} **[+ pps_sejm_display +]** {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#C96A24'> </div></td><td>!} NPR {!</td><td>!} [+ npr_sejm_display +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#6FAF45'> </div></td><td>!} PSL Wyzwolenie {!</td><td>!} [+ psl_wyzwolenie_sejm_display +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#2F7D32'> </div></td><td>!} PSL Piast {!</td><td>!} [+ psl_piast_sejm_display +] {!</td></tr>!}
[? if not sejm_has_chzjn : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#D5AC27'> </div></td><td>!} PSChD {!</td><td>!} [+ pschd_sejm_display +] {!</td></tr>!} ?]
[? if not sejm_has_chzjn : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#3F7BC1'> </div></td><td>!} [+ zln_name +] {!</td><td>!} [+ zln_sejm_display +] {!</td></tr>!} ?]
[? if sejm_has_chzjn : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#3F7BC1'> </div></td><td>!} ChZJN (ZLN + PSChD) {!</td><td>!} [+ chzjn_sejm_display +] {!</td></tr>!} ?]
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#7C5AA6'> </div></td><td>!} [? if opening_sejm_active : Minority deputies ?][? if not opening_sejm_active : Blok Mniejszości Narodowych ?] {!</td><td>!} [+ minorities_bloc_sejm_display +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#A0A0A0'> </div></td><td>!} Inne {!</td><td>!} [+ other_sejm_display +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!</table>!}

